The 512-channel / 128-layer positive-control shape is inspired by the ANEMLL
benchmark and related maderix/ANE work. LLMs on Apple Neural Engine uses a separately generated
Hadamard/sign/permutation fixture and explicit numerical/device controls. See:
https://gist.github.com/Anemll/49e219448ad350ef67ff4bfdcb9ebd8c
https://github.com/maderix/ANE

Apple Core ML, Core AI, coremltools and coreai-torch supply APIs used by the
adapters. PyTorch and NumPy supply authoring and reference arithmetic. Dependencies
are installed separately and retain their own licenses; no dependency source,
model weights, Apple framework binaries or compiled models are redistributed.
Core AI private Python authoring/bytecode interfaces are version-pinned.

